   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "title",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Airline Passenger Satisfaction — Bivariate Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook visualizes the relationship between overall satisfaction and the variables required for the three predefined hypotheses. It is intentionally descriptive: **no hypothesis tests, p-values, confidence intervals, regression models, or statistical-significance conclusions are included**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The plots address:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Service ratings and satisfaction\n",
    "2. Travel class and satisfaction\n",
    "3. Flight delays and satisfaction"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "setup",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-13T06:55:52.154155Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-13T06:55:52.153881Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-13T06:55:53.161644Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-13T06:55:53.161262Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Loaded 129,880 passenger records and 70 columns.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from IPython.display import Markdown, display\n",
    "from matplotlib.ticker import PercentFormatter\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\", context=\"notebook\")\n",
    "COLORS = sns.color_palette(\"colorblind\")\n",
    "SATISFACTION_COLORS = {\"Satisfied\": COLORS[2], \"Neutral or Dissatisfied\": COLORS[1]}\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\"figure.dpi\": 110, \"axes.titleweight\": \"bold\"})\n",
    "\n",
    "PROJECT_ROOT = Path.cwd().parent if Path.cwd().name == \"notebooks\" else Path.cwd()\n",
    "DATA_PATH = PROJECT_ROOT / \"data/processed/airline_passenger_satisfaction_cleaned.csv\"\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(df):,} passenger records and {df.shape[1]} columns.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "scope",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Scope and analysis conventions\n",
    "\n",
    "- `is_satisfied = 1` represents **Satisfied**; `0` represents **Neutral or Dissatisfied**.\n",
    "- Clean service-rating fields treat undocumented zero ratings as missing.\n",
    "- Counts and denominators are displayed so percentage differences can be interpreted in context.\n",
    "- Delay outliers are retained. Distribution plots use a 99th-percentile viewing limit only for readability.\n",
    "- Observed differences are descriptive associations and are not evidence of causation or statistical significance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "helpers",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-13T06:55:53.162916Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-13T06:55:53.162846Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-13T06:55:53.165715Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-13T06:55:53.165378Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def outcome_summary(group_column, order=None):\n",
    "    result = (\n",
    "        df.groupby(group_column, dropna=False, observed=True)\n",
    "        .agg(Passengers=(\"passenger_id\", \"size\"), Satisfied=(\"is_satisfied\", \"sum\"), Satisfaction_rate=(\"is_satisfied\", \"mean\"))\n",
    "        .reset_index()\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    result[\"Neutral_or_dissatisfied\"] = result[\"Passengers\"] - result[\"Satisfied\"]\n",
    "    if order is not None:\n",
    "        result[group_column] = pd.Categorical(result[group_column], categories=order, ordered=True)\n",
    "        result = result.sort_values(group_column).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "    return result\n",
    "\n",
    "def display_outcome_table(table):\n",
    "    display(table.style.format({\n",
    "        \"Passengers\": \"{:,}\", \"Satisfied\": \"{:,}\",\n",
    "        \"Neutral_or_dissatisfied\": \"{:,}\", \"Satisfaction_rate\": \"{:.1%}\"\n",
    "    }).hide(axis=\"index\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "def annotate_rates(ax):\n",
    "    for patch in ax.patches:\n",
    "        height = patch.get_height()\n",
    "        if np.isfinite(height):\n",
    "            ax.text(patch.get_x() + patch.get_width()/2, height, f\"{height:.1%}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=9)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "h1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Hypothesis 1 variables: service quality and satisfaction\n",
    "\n",
    "The first hypothesis concerns cleanliness, seat comfort, and onboard service. The following charts show how the observed satisfaction rate and satisfaction composition vary across each clean rating level."
   ]
  },
